-- A module with NO import relationship to `gradedmod` whatsoever.  Its `f` is an
-- ordinary higher-kinded type variable that merely SHARES THE SPELLING of
-- GThenable's row-indexed head, at the same arity.
--
-- ⚠️ Two details are the whole fixture, and BOTH were got wrong in a first draft
-- that pinned nothing (identical output before and after the fix):
--   * the head must be spelled `f` — the leaked key was the bare typaram NAME, so a
--     head named `g` never collided;
--   * the first argument must be a CONCRETE type, not a variable.  A leaked Row slot
--     holding a type variable becomes an OPEN row, which the scheme renderer prints
--     exactly like a type variable — `a b c -> a b c` either way.  A leaked Row slot
--     holding `Int` erases to `<>` (rowArgOf's catch-all), which is visible.
export keep : f Int a -> f Int a
keep x = x
